nodecode-gonogo is a rewrite of keppy's keppy/hermes-plugin-gonogo:
https://github.com/keppy/hermes-plugin-gonogo
commit faf3e6a5f905522359e2fc7ab3468c814d00db01

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 James Dominguez (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's three tools (gonogo_decide, gonogo_report,
gonogo_compare) as the eval-callable verbs gonogo:decide, gonogo:report and
gonogo:compare, and the reading of a results file (JSONL rows, or a saved
report JSON) into trials -- error cases, abstentions, expected actions,
groups, per-case confidence. The Python dependency gonogo-eval is gone: its
statistics are reimplemented here in Common Lisp -- the Wilson score interval
and the z values behind it, the sample size a rate would need, the
risk-coverage curve and the threshold whose precision lower bound clears the
target, expected calibration error, McNemar's exact test with the
simultaneous-Wilson interval on the difference, and the five verdicts with
their wording and ordering.

What was left out: the bundled skill (skills/gonogo-verdict/SKILL.md) is
documentation for the model, so its wording lives in the cell's manual and
README rather than as a separate skill file; the HTML report is a plain page
around the markdown instead of the library's styled one; the actions table is
reduced to its two counts (acted when it should have held back, held back when
it should have acted) rather than the full expected-by-taken matrix; and the
gonogo Python API itself (Case, Prediction, evaluate, the CLI) is not
exposed, since the verdict is the whole of what the plugin gave a session.
